 61CU    28SI(36AR,3PG):XUNDL-3        2008AN06                           200806
 61CU c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2008An06:                          
 61CU2c  Eur Phys Jour A 36, 251 (2008)                                         
 61CU c  Compiled by S. Geraedts and B. Singh (McMaster); June 26, 2008         
 61CU c  Three experiments were performed: GS54, GSFMA42 and FSFMA138. All      
 61CU2c  experiments using the GAMMASPHERE array to measured E|g, I|g,          
 61CU3c  |g|g, (particle)|g coin, |g|g(|q)(DCO). The protons and |a particles   
 61CU4c  were detected using the MICROBALL array and Si strip telescopes used   
 61CU5c  for |DE-E measurements. Comparisons with cranked Nilsson and Strutinsky
 61CU6c  model calculations for collective structures and with large-scale      
 61CU7c  shell-model calculations for normal-deformed states.                   
 61CU t  ---------------------------------------------------------------------- 
 61CU t  Experiment            GS54           GSFMA42              GSFMA138     
 61CU t  ---------------------------------------------------------------------- 
 61CU t  Beam energy           143 MeV         148 MeV              142 MeV     
 61CU t  Ge detectors          82              86                   77          
 61CU t  Microball elements    95              65                   16          
 61CU t  Si |DE-E telescopes   --              4                    8           
 61CU t  Liquid scintillators  15              20                   30          
 61CU t  (for neutrons)                                                         
 61CU t  Laboratory            LBNL            Argonne              Argonne     
 61CU t  ---------------------------------------------------------------------- 
 61CU cG $ DCO values are for 30|'-83|' geometry with gates on |DJ=2, quadrupole
 61CU2cG and |DJ=1, dipole transitions. Expected values of DCO's are: 1. for    
 61CU3cG gate on |DJ=2, quadrupole: 1.0 for |DJ=2, quadrupole; |<1.0 for |DJ=0  
 61CU4cG and |?0.6 for |DJ=1 transitions. 2. for gate on |DJ=1, dipole          
 61CU5cG transitions: |?1.0 for |DJ=1, dipole; 1.7 for |DJ=2, quadrupole or     
 61CU6cG |DJ=0, dipole.                                                         
 61CU cG $ DCO(1) corresponds to value for gate on |DJ=2, quadrupole and        
 61CU2cG DCO(2) for gate on |DJ=1, dipole. One DCO value is for gate on |DJ=0   
 61CU3cG transition, as indicated.                                              
 61CU cG E(X)$ DCO value is for an unresolved doublet                           
